# Fusion OS package additions (appended to the archiso releng list).
# Target: a weak x86-64 laptop. Lean gaming stack, no heavy desktop.

# --- Graphics drivers: open stack for all common laptop GPUs ---
mesa
lib32-mesa
vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-radeon          # AMD
lib32-vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel           # Intel
lib32-vulkan-intel
vulkan-nouveau         # NVIDIA (open). Proprietary = see iso/README (nvidia).
mesa-utils
libva-mesa-driver

# --- Gaming runtime ---
steam
gamescope
mangohud
lib32-mangohud
gamemode
lib32-gamemode
wine
wine-gecko
wine-mono
winetricks
vkd3d
lib32-vkd3d
dxvk-bin               # (AUR) or install per-prefix via the Compatibility Manager

# --- Controllers / input ---
xpadneo-dkms           # xbox pads (AUR/community); DS4 is handled by hid-sony in-kernel
# dualsensectl         # optional, DualSense extras

# --- System / performance ---
zram-generator
power-profiles-daemon
irqbalance
mesa-demos

# --- Preinstalled apps (NOT part of setup; launch on demand) ---
firefox                # browser
discord                # official Linux client
flatpak                # used to install Heroic (Epic/GOG) universally at first boot
# Steam is already in the gaming runtime section above -- it comes installed but
# the setup wizard never asks for a Steam/cloud account; sign in only if you want.
# Epic Games has NO native Linux client; Heroic Games Launcher is the standard
# way to run Epic titles. Installed via flatpak by fusion-firstboot (see notes).

# --- Install-to-disk ---
archinstall

# --- Base niceties on a weak box ---
python                 # the Fusion tools need only python3 (already in base)
htop
nano
sudo
networkmanager
